{"format":"hologram.registry.artifact/v1","id":"mcr.microsoft.com/azurelinux/distroless/prometheus-adapter","fetched":"2026-09-25T12:12:08.188Z","source":{"name":"Microsoft Artifact Registry","api":"https://mcr.microsoft.com/api/v1/catalog/azurelinux/distroless/prometheus-adapter/details?reg=mar","page":"https://mcr.microsoft.com/en-us/product/azurelinux/distroless/prometheus-adapter/about"},"readme":"## About\n\nThis repository contains the official Prometheus-Adapter image for Azure Linux.\n\n### What is Azure Linux?\n\nAzure Linux is a Linux distribution for Microsoft’s cloud infrastructure and edge products and services. Azure Linux is designed to provide a consistent platform for these devices and services and will enhance Microsoft’s ability to stay current on Linux updates.  \n\nTo learn more about Azure Linux, refer to our [GitHub repository](https://github.com/microsoft/azurelinux/).\n\n### What is Prometheus-Adapter?\n\nPrometheus-Adapter is a project that implements the Kubernetes Custom, Resource, and External Metric APIs in such a way that they integrate Prometheus metrics logging, allowing Kubernetes clusters to easily use Prometheus-Adapter for logging and monitoring.\n\nSee: [https://github.com/kubernetes-sigs/prometheus-adapter/blob/master/README.md](https://github.com/kubernetes-sigs/prometheus-adapter/blob/master/README.md).\n\n## Featured tags\n\n- `0`\n- `0.12`\n\nThe featured tags are multi-architecture tags (i.e., `x86-64` and `aarch64`) that refer to the latest version of the image. Additional tags that are specific to Prometheus-Adapter version, Azure Linux build, or architecture can be found in the Tags section.\n\n## Usage\n\n### Running a Prometheus-Adapter container (Assuming an existing Kubernetes project)\n\n`1.` Run the Azure Linux Prometheus-Adapter container image with custom config file mounted.\n\n    docker run -it --rm mcr.microsoft.com/azurelinux/base/prometheus-adapter:0.12 <input params>\n\n    docker run -it --rm mcr.microsoft.com/azurelinux/distroless/prometheus-adapter:0.12 <input params>\n    \nThe container entrypoint is `adapter`, so the user needs to supply arguments like the config file, etc.\n\n## Support\n\nAzure Linux container images are supported only for internal Microsoft use. For more information please see our [Support Statement](https://github.com/microsoft/azurelinux/blob/-/SUPPORT.md).\n\n## License\n\nThe Azure Linux distribution is provided under the [MIT license](https://github.com/microsoft/azurelinux/blob/-/LICENSE). Individual packages and components are governed by their own licenses included in the package sources available via srpm on [packages.microsoft.com](https://packages.microsoft.com/azurelinux/) or via our [GitHub repository](https://github.com/microsoft/azurelinux/).\n\n- Legal Notice: [Container License Information](https://aka.ms/mcr/osslegalnotice)","readmeBase":null,"publisher":{"name":"Microsoft","url":"https://mcr.microsoft.com/","official":true,"verified":true},"registered":null,"updated":"2026-09-12T02:12:43.7175505+00:00","categories":[],"keywords":[],"license":"MIT","links":[],"maintainers":[],"stats":{"pulls":null,"pullsText":"111K+","stars":null},"mediaTypes":[],"contentTypes":[],"storage":null,"tags":[{"name":"0.12-debug-nonroot","digest":"sha256:67ca9bebca90b8919223bef3a83edc176c29058733f37a517a3543892719621c","pushed":"2026-09-12T01:53:09.0000000+00:00","size":null,"platforms":[],"mediaType":"application/vnd.docker.distribution.manifest.list.v2+json","status":null},{"name":"0-debug-nonroot","digest":"sha256:67ca9bebca90b8919223bef3a83edc176c29058733f37a517a3543892719621c","pushed":"2026-09-12T01:53:05.0000000+00:00","size":null,"platforms":[],"mediaType":"application/vnd.docker.distribution.manifest.list.v2+json","status":null},{"name":"0.12.0-9-debug-nonroot-azl3.0.20260909","digest":"sha256:67ca9bebca90b8919223bef3a83edc176c29058733f37a517a3543892719621c","pushed":"2026-09-12T01:52:59.0000000+00:00","size":null,"platforms":[],"mediaT